silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_flat_sections_04_three_substrates_concrete_anchor_4#mittenssourcediagram silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensSourceDiagram is the source diagram whose ten typed legs are record, identifier, quality, measurement, role, process, validation, trace, classification, taxonomy. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
